# Orbs · Design and implementation kit · v1.0 · FINAL RING DIRECTION
10 October 2026. Hackathon handoff. Mobile + web.

## Direction
Content stays primary. Orbs appears at the point of attention, carries context into a spoken request, and returns a small actionable card. Monochrome, fine-line, calm, compact. Avoid dashboards, full-screen chat takeovers, neon glows, glass blur, decorative gradients, and large assistant avatars.

References reviewed: supplied 23.9-second eye-tracking + voice recording; all eleven supplied screenshots; https://libraries.dev/orbs. Phone footage demonstrates gaze as additional probabilistic context, not a command. Dark screenshots supply fine-line orb forms and compact pill/card composition. Colored heatmaps and blue/green UI accents are translated to grayscale to meet this kit's monochrome requirement. Values below are new implementation decisions, not extracted measurements.

## Files
- index.html — self-contained animated visual guide. Open directly in any modern browser.
- tokens.css — production tokens and small reusable component styles.
- OrbsIndicator.tsx — React adapter using the exact thinking-orbs component.
- tokens.json — platform-neutral tokens, including typography and motion.
- orb-motion.css — selected pulse, rotation and burst animations. Import alongside OrbsIndicator.tsx.

## Color
Light: canvas #FAFAFA, surface #FFFFFF, raised #F4F4F4, text #171717, secondary #666666, border #DEDEDE. Dark: canvas #111111, surface #1A1A1A, raised #242424, text #F5F5F5, secondary #AAAAAA, border #383838. Black and white establish the identity; grays express hierarchy. Use text and icons for success, warning and error; no color-only status. Never place small gray labels over animated orb lines.

## Typography
System sans: SF on Apple; Segoe UI on Windows; system fallback elsewhere. No font downloads required. Product wordmark: Orbs, medium, -0.04em; use text rather than a fabricated logo asset.
Display 48/52 weight 500, -0.04em (mobile 36/40). Section 28/34 weight 500, -0.025em. Card title 18/24 weight 600, -0.015em. Body 15/22 weight 400. Control 14/20 weight 500. Metadata 12/16 weight 500. Native units are points; web units pixels. Honor native Dynamic Type / web zoom; do not lock card heights.

## Layout
Spacing grid: 4,8,12,16,20,24,32,48,64. Screen gutter 20 mobile / 32 desktop. Card padding 20; nested rows 12; gaps 8 or 12. Card radius 24; controls 12; pills 999. Fine 1px borders. Shadow only on floating surfaces. 44px minimum interaction targets, including any visible 20px icon. Card widths: web 360 (max 400), mobile viewport minus 32px. Cards grow vertically with content.

## Attention / initial heatmap
Default product view shows no heatmap. On hover, focus, touch selection or gaze candidate, show a single soft grayscale patch (8% ink, 18px blur) plus a fine outline once selected. Debug mode may reveal raw attention intensity; label it Debug, keep it separate from the product default. Gaze is evidence, not authorization. For this day's demo, hover/tap may simulate attention; label simulation in the demo. An approximate 350ms dwell can expose a candidate but must be calibrated; voice or explicit selection commits context. Keep text readable and do not track gaze across apps without implemented support.

## Orb anatomy and selected state contract
Final choice: Ring, as shown in the approved screenshot (10 October, 14:35). All states use the exact thinking-orbs 0.3.2 breathing geometry. Never switch to composing, working or listening geometry. Keep the 64px hero and 20px inline library presets. A wrapper introduces distinct motion without replacing the library renderer. Status labels remain mandatory.

| App state | Library state | Speed / dotSize | Wrapper movement | Label |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Idle | breathing | .3 / .8 | slow native drift | Ready |
| Listening | breathing | .65 / 1 | irregular scale .88–1.2 over 2.6s | Listening… |
| Thinking | breathing | .75 / 1 | continuous 360° rotation, 4.5s linear | Thinking… |
| Acting | breathing | 1.2 / 1.15 | three 120° forward bursts, 2.2s, scale 1–1.12 | Actual tool activity |
| Confirmation | breathing, paused | .3 / .8 | static | Ready to add |
| Done | breathing, paused | .3 / .8 | static + adjacent check | Added to your calendar |
| Error | breathing, paused | .3 / .8 | static + adjacent warning | Calendar unavailable · Retry |

Listening pulse is the approved illustrative rhythm, not microphone-driven. Render it only while recording. If implementing audio reactivity later, replace its wrapper scale with normalized RMS, clamped to .88–1.2; leave breathing geometry intact. Hero slot needs 12px motion clearance on each side (64 × 1.2 = 76.8px). Inline orb sits inside a minimum 44px pill. Motion changes have a distinct rhythm, rather than speed alone.

State path: Idle → Listening → Thinking → Acting → Confirmation (for writes) → Acting → Done. Cancel returns Idle; failure enters Error. User correction can return Listening. Read-only results may go Acting → Done directly. No fake progress, fabricated success, or invented completion percentages. After 8s show 'Still checking…'; after 20s show cancel/retry if backend supports it. Keep truthful text when tools take longer.

## Cards
1. Context: small source chip + user's interpreted request; edit/change target available.
2. Result: one sentence outcome; up to three information rows; source attribution.
3. Confirmation: summarize exact writes and affected objects; primary Confirm, secondary Cancel.
4. Done: report confirmed changes; Undo only if backend provides reversal.
5. Error: what failed, preserved context, Retry/Cancel.
Desktop: anchored 12px from target, flip to keep 16px viewport margin; clamp to viewport, close on Escape and restore trigger focus. Mobile: bottom contextual sheet above keyboard and safe area with 16px side margins. No dim backdrop for passive results; modal confirmation may use 20% black scrim, dialog semantics and trapped focus. Scroll result content when height exceeds 60vh. Voice transcript remains editable; text input remains available.

## Motion
Enter: 320ms cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1), opacity 0→1, y 8→0px, scale .98→1. Exit: 160ms cubic-bezier(.4,0,1,1), opacity 1→0, y 0→4px. State change: 200ms cubic-bezier(.4,0,.2,1). Control feedback:120ms. Native equivalents can use cubic timing curves; avoid spring overshoot. Orbs can loop linearly internally; never bounce the whole card. Animate transforms/opacity; pause offscreen. Reduced motion: static orb, persistent textual state, immediate placement with optional 100ms opacity fade. No essential state conveyed only through animation.

## Accessibility
Visible labels for all states. role=status / aria-live=polite for status text, not a per-frame announcement. Canvas aria-hidden when adjacent text duplicates it. Modal confirmation uses role=dialog, labelled title, focus trap, Escape and restored focus. Keyboard selection offers same context as hover. Maintain body contrast ≥4.5:1; large text ≥3:1. Focus ring 2px with 3px offset. Debug attention layer pointer-events:none. Microphone button has explicit accessible name and recording state. Do not auto-record.

## Using the selected exact library component
npm install thinking-orbs@0.3.2 react react-dom

```tsx
import { OrbsIndicator } from './OrbsIndicator';
<OrbsIndicator state="thinking" size={64} dark={false} reducedMotion={false} />
```

OrbsIndicator imports orb-motion.css. Internally it always renders <ThinkingOrb state="breathing" size={64} /> (or 20) with state-specific speed and dotSize props. Theme is theme="dark" / theme="light". Supply reducedMotion from your app's hook; the CSS also honors the OS preference. All wrappers stop for confirmation, done and error. Use check/warning icons and visible text beside them. The standalone guide bundles React and the exact library and opens offline. MIT notices included. No custom geometry renderer remains.

## Demo acceptance checklist
- Mobile 390px and desktop 1440px, no overflow; zoom 200% remains usable.
- Exact 64px hero and 20px inline presets, no stretch or color overrides.
- Listening only during capture; acting labels reflect actual tools.
- Confirmation before changes; actual success before Done.
- Cancel, error, empty and reduced-motion views remain understandable.
- Mobile safe areas + keyboard placement checked on target device.
import SwiftUI
import UIKit

/// The Orb Agent design system for the iPhone app, from the team's design tokens
/// (Paper "Micro Intent - Hackathon Prototypes", page "Design System", variant D dark glass).
/// Dark values are the tokens as given; the light values are their counterparts so cards
/// and chrome also read well in light mode.
enum Theme {
    // MARK: Ground

    /// `color.canvas` from brand kit tokens.json: #FAFAFA light, #111111 dark.
    static let canvas = Color(light: 0xFAFAFA, dark: 0x111111)
    static let canvasBottom = Color(light: 0xFAFAFA, dark: 0x111111)

    // MARK: Surfaces & Brand Colors (`tokens.json`)

    /// `color.surface`: #FFFFFF light, #1A1A1A dark.
    static let surface = Color(light: 0xFFFFFF, dark: 0x1A1A1A)
    /// `color.raised`: #F4F4F4 light, #242424 dark.
    static let raised = Color(light: 0xF4F4F4, dark: 0x242424)
    /// `color.border`: #DEDEDE light, #383838 dark.
    static let border = Color(light: 0xDEDEDE, dark: 0x383838)
    /// Selection highlight: 7% ink in light, 10% ink in dark.
    static let selected = Color(light: 0x171717, lightAlpha: 0.07, dark: 0xFFFFFF, darkAlpha: 0.10)

    // MARK: Surface Mappings (Legacy compatibility)

    static let surfaceCard = surface
    static let surfaceChip = raised
    static let surfaceControl = raised
    static let surfaceInput = surface
    static let borderInput = border
    static let borderSubtle = border
    static let borderGlass = border
    static let borderLine = border

    static let glassPanel = surface
    static let glassPill = surface
    static let glassSheet = surface
    static let glassHighlight = Color.clear

    /// Shadow only on floating surfaces (brand kit: 0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,.08) light, .28 dark).
    static let shadow = Color(light: 0x000000, lightAlpha: 0.08, dark: 0x000000, darkAlpha: 0.28)
    static let shadowPanel = shadow
    static let shadowPill = shadow

    // MARK: Text (`tokens.json`)

    /// `color.text`: #171717 light, #F5F5F5 dark.
    static let textPrimary = Color(light: 0x171717, dark: 0xF5F5F5)
    /// `color.secondary`: #666666 light, #AAAAAA dark.
    static let textSecondary = Color(light: 0x666666, dark: 0xAAAAAA)
    static let textTertiary = textSecondary
    static let textMuted = textSecondary
    static let textPlaceholder = Color(light: 0x666666, lightAlpha: 0.6, dark: 0xAAAAAA, darkAlpha: 0.6)

    // MARK: Monochrome Identity & Status
    // Monochrome: Black and white establish identity; grays express hierarchy.
    // Status uses text + check/warning icons, never color-only.

    static let accent = textPrimary
    static let accentStrong = textPrimary
    static let accentText = textPrimary
    static let accentTextStrong = textPrimary
    static let accentSoft = selected
    static let accentBorder = border

    static let successText = textPrimary
    static let successSoft = selected
    static let warnText = textPrimary
    static let warnSoft = selected
    static let dangerText = textPrimary
    static let dangerSoft = selected

    // MARK: Orb Presets (preserved for OrbView renderer)

    enum Orb {
        static let core: [Gradient.Stop] = [
            .init(color: Color(hex: 0xFFFFFF), location: 0),
            .init(color: Color(hex: 0xCFF4FF), location: 0.16),
            .init(color: Color(hex: 0x6FB8FF), location: 0.44),
            .init(color: Color(hex: 0x2F6BFF), location: 0.72),
            .init(color: Color(hex: 0x1B3BD1), location: 1),
        ]
        static let idle: [Gradient.Stop] = [
            .init(color: Color(hex: 0xFFFFFF), location: 0),
            .init(color: Color(hex: 0xE4E9F2), location: 0.4),
            .init(color: Color(hex: 0xB9C2D6), location: 1),
        ]
        static let thinking = [Color(hex: 0x1B3BD1), Color(hex: 0x6FB8FF), Color(hex: 0xFFFFFF), Color(hex: 0x2F6BFF), Color(hex: 0x1B3BD1)]
        static let thinkingStart: Double = 200
        static let glow = Color(hex: 0x3E8BFF)
        static let ring = Color(light: 0x3D63FF, dark: 0x9DBBFF)
        static let idleEdge = Color(light: 0x8FA0C4, lightAlpha: 0.45, dark: 0xFFFFFF, darkAlpha: 0)
        static let innerShade = Color(hex: 0x0A145A)
        static let hero: CGFloat = 64
        static let inline: CGFloat = 20
    }

    // MARK: Radii & Sizes (`tokens.json`)

    enum Radius {
        static let card: CGFloat = 24
        static let control: CGFloat = 12
        static let pill: CGFloat = 999

        // Legacy aliases
        static let sm: CGFloat = 8
        static let md: CGFloat = 12
        static let lg: CGFloat = 12
        static let xl: CGFloat = 18
        static let xxl: CGFloat = 24
        static let xxxl: CGFloat = 24
    }

    enum Size {
        static let touchMin: CGFloat = 44
        static let pillHeight: CGFloat = 44
        static let inputHeight: CGFloat = 44
        static let cardGutterMobile: CGFloat = 16
        static let cardPadding: CGFloat = 20
    }

    // MARK: Motion (`tokens.json`)

    enum Motion {
        static let enterMs = 320
        static let exitMs = 160
        static let standardMs = 200
        static let feedbackMs = 120

        static let enterDuration = 0.32
        static let exitDuration = 0.16
        static let standardDuration = 0.20
        static let feedbackDuration = 0.12

        static let enter = Animation.timingCurve(0.16, 1.0, 0.3, 1.0, duration: 0.32)
        static let exit = Animation.timingCurve(0.4, 0.0, 1.0, 1.0, duration: 0.16)
        static let standard = Animation.timingCurve(0.4, 0.0, 0.2, 1.0, duration: 0.20)

        // Legacy compatibility
        static let fast = 0.12
        static let base = 0.20
        static let panel = 0.32
        static let breathe = 4.0
        static let listen = 2.6
        static let think = 4.5
        static let speak = 2.2
    }
}

// MARK: - Typography

/// System SF scale exactly matching brand kit tokens.json:
/// display (mobile 36/40 weight 500), section (28/34 weight 500),
/// cardTitle (18/24 weight 600), body (15/22 weight 400),
/// control (14/20 weight 500), metadata (12/16 weight 500).
struct TypeScale {
    let name: String
    let display: Font
    let section: Font
    let cardTitle: Font
    let body: Font
    let bodyStrong: Font
    let button: Font
    let control: CGFloat
    let label: Font
    let meta: Font
    let eyebrow: Font
    let eyebrowTracking: CGFloat
    let time: Font
    let answer: Font
    let answerTracking: CGFloat

    static let regular = TypeScale(
        name: "regular",
        display: .system(size: 36, weight: .medium),
        section: .system(size: 28, weight: .medium),
        cardTitle: .system(size: 18, weight: .semibold),
        body: .system(size: 15, weight: .regular),
        bodyStrong: .system(size: 15, weight: .semibold),
        button: .system(size: 14, weight: .medium),
        control: 44,
        label: .system(size: 14, weight: .medium),
        meta: .system(size: 12, weight: .medium),
        eyebrow: .system(size: 12, weight: .medium),
        eyebrowTracking: 0.5,
        time: .system(size: 18, weight: .semibold),
        answer: .system(size: 28, weight: .medium),
        answerTracking: -0.7
    )

    static let large = TypeScale(
        name: "large",
        display: .system(size: 42, weight: .medium),
        section: .system(size: 34, weight: .medium),
        cardTitle: .system(size: 22, weight: .semibold),
        body: .system(size: 18, weight: .regular),
        bodyStrong: .system(size: 18, weight: .semibold),
        button: .system(size: 16, weight: .medium),
        control: 52,
        label: .system(size: 16, weight: .medium),
        meta: .system(size: 14, weight: .medium),
        eyebrow: .system(size: 14, weight: .medium),
        eyebrowTracking: 0.5,
        time: .system(size: 22, weight: .semibold),
        answer: .system(size: 34, weight: .medium),
        answerTracking: -0.8
    )
}

private struct TypeScaleKey: EnvironmentKey {
    static let defaultValue = TypeScale.regular
}

extension EnvironmentValues {
    var typeScale: TypeScale {
        get { self[TypeScaleKey.self] }
        set { self[TypeScaleKey.self] = newValue }
    }
}

// MARK: - Color helpers

extension Color {
    init(hex: UInt32, alpha: Double = 1) {
        self.init(
            .sRGB,
            red: Double((hex >> 16) & 0xFF) / 255,
            green: Double((hex >> 8) & 0xFF) / 255,
            blue: Double(hex & 0xFF) / 255,
            opacity: alpha
        )
    }

    init(light: UInt32, lightAlpha: Double = 1, dark: UInt32, darkAlpha: Double = 1) {
        self.init(uiColor: UIColor { traits in
            traits.userInterfaceStyle == .dark
                ? UIColor(Color(hex: dark, alpha: darkAlpha))
                : UIColor(Color(hex: light, alpha: lightAlpha))
        })
    }
}

// MARK: - Surfaces & Liquid Glass

/// Floating Liquid Glass surface on iOS 26 with fallback to .ultraThinMaterial on older iOS.
/// Fine 1px border, shadow only on floating surfaces.
struct GlassSurface: ViewModifier {
    enum Kind { case panel, pill, flat }
    var kind: Kind = .panel
    var cornerRadius: CGFloat = Theme.Radius.card
    var isInteractive: Bool = false

    func body(content: Content) -> some View {
        let shape = RoundedRectangle(cornerRadius: cornerRadius, style: .continuous)
        if #available(iOS 26.0, *) {
            content
                .glassEffect(isInteractive ? .regular.interactive() : .regular)
                .clipShape(shape)
                .overlay(shape.strokeBorder(Theme.border, lineWidth: 1))
                .shadow(
                    color: kind == .flat ? .clear : Theme.shadow,
                    radius: kind == .panel ? 16 : 8,
                    y: kind == .panel ? 8 : 4
                )
        } else {
            content
                .background {
                    shape
                        .fill(.ultraThinMaterial)
                        .overlay(shape.fill(kind == .panel ? Theme.surface.opacity(0.9) : Theme.raised.opacity(0.85)))
                }
                .overlay(shape.strokeBorder(Theme.border, lineWidth: 1))
                .shadow(
                    color: kind == .flat ? .clear : Theme.shadow,
                    radius: kind == .panel ? 16 : 8,
                    y: kind == .panel ? 8 : 4
                )
        }
    }
}

extension View {
    func glassSurface(_ kind: GlassSurface.Kind = .panel, cornerRadius: CGFloat = Theme.Radius.card, isInteractive: Bool = false) -> some View {
        modifier(GlassSurface(kind: kind, cornerRadius: cornerRadius, isInteractive: isInteractive))
    }

    /// Small uppercase label above content, `text.eyebrow`.
    func eyebrow(_ scale: TypeScale, color: Color = Theme.textMuted) -> some View {
        font(scale.eyebrow).tracking(scale.eyebrowTracking).textCase(.uppercase).foregroundStyle(color)
    }
}

/// Buttons from the kit:
/// Primary button = text color filled (`Theme.textPrimary`), text in `Theme.surface`.
/// Secondary button = raised with 1px border (`Theme.raised`, `Theme.border`).
/// Controls have radius 12, minimum height 44pt.
struct BigButtonStyle: ButtonStyle {
    enum Kind { case primary, secondary }
    var kind: Kind

    @Environment(\.isEnabled) private var isEnabled
    @Environment(\.typeScale) private var type
    @Environment(\.accessibilityReduceMotion) private var reduceMotion

    func makeBody(configuration: Configuration) -> some View {
        let shape = RoundedRectangle(cornerRadius: Theme.Radius.control, style: .continuous)
        configuration.label
            .font(type.button)
            .foregroundStyle(kind == .primary ? Theme.surface : Theme.textPrimary)
            .frame(maxWidth: .infinity, minHeight: max(Theme.Size.touchMin, type.control))
            .background {
                if kind == .primary {
                    shape.fill(Theme.textPrimary)
                } else {
                    shape.fill(Theme.raised)
                }
            }
            .overlay {
                if kind == .secondary {
                    shape.strokeBorder(Theme.border, lineWidth: 1)
                }
            }
            .opacity(isEnabled ? (configuration.isPressed ? 0.8 : 1) : 0.4)
            .scaleEffect(reduceMotion ? 1 : (configuration.isPressed ? 0.98 : 1))
            .animation(reduceMotion ? nil : .easeOut(duration: Theme.Motion.fast), value: configuration.isPressed)
    }
}

/// Calm monochrome background; no neon glow or decorative gradients.
struct AppBackground: View {
    var glow: Double = 1

    var body: some View {
        Theme.canvas
            .ignoresSafeArea()
    }
}

import SwiftUI

/// The one screen: screen chip, the latest turn (question, mascot line, cards), and the orb.
struct ContentView: View {
    @Bindable var session: AgentSession
    @Binding var sheet: AppSheet?

    @Environment(\.typeScale) private var type
    @State private var pressing = false
    @State private var debugHold: Task<Void, Never>?
    @Namespace private var glassNamespace

    var body: some View {
        Group {
            if #available(iOS 26.0, *) {
                GlassEffectContainer {
                    contentLayout
                }
            } else {
                contentLayout
            }
        }
        .background(AppBackground())
    }

    private var contentLayout: some View {
        VStack(spacing: 0) {
            topBar
            ScrollView {
                VStack(alignment: .leading, spacing: 14) {
                    if let screen = session.screen {
                        ScreenChip(summary: screen.summary)
                            .transition(.move(edge: .top).combined(with: .opacity))
                    }
                    turn
                }
                .frame(maxWidth: .infinity, alignment: .leading)
                .padding(.horizontal, Theme.Size.cardGutterMobile)
                .padding(.top, 8)
                .padding(.bottom, 28)
                .animation(Theme.Motion.standard, value: session.screen)
                .animation(Theme.Motion.standard, value: session.reply)
                .animation(Theme.Motion.standard, value: session.confirmation)
                .animation(Theme.Motion.standard, value: session.doneMessage)
            }
            .scrollIndicators(.hidden)
            .mask {
                // Cards fade out where they scroll under the orb.
                VStack(spacing: 0) {
                    Color.black
                    LinearGradient(colors: [.black, .clear], startPoint: .top, endPoint: .bottom)
                        .frame(height: 20)
                }
            }
            orbDock
        }
    }

    // MARK: - Top bar

    private var topBar: some View {
        HStack(spacing: 12) {
            Text("Orb Agent")
                .font(.system(size: 20, weight: .medium))
                .tracking(-0.8)
                .foregroundStyle(Theme.textPrimary)
            Spacer()
            ConnectionBadge(connection: session.connection)
            Button {
                sheet = .settings
            } label: {
                Image(systemName: "gearshape")
                    .font(.system(size: 18, weight: .medium))
                    .foregroundStyle(Theme.textPrimary)
                    .frame(width: Theme.Size.touchMin, height: Theme.Size.touchMin)
                    .glassSurface(.flat, cornerRadius: Theme.Radius.control, isInteractive: true)
            }
            .accessibilityLabel("Settings")
        }
        .padding(.horizontal, Theme.Size.cardGutterMobile)
        .padding(.vertical, 8)
    }

    // MARK: - Latest turn

    @ViewBuilder
    private var turn: some View {
        if let transcript = session.transcript {
            Text("“\(transcript)”")
                .font(type.bodyStrong)
                .foregroundStyle(Theme.textMuted)
                .fixedSize(horizontal: false, vertical: true)
                .padding(.horizontal, 4)
        }
        if let confirmation = session.confirmation {
            ConfirmationCard(
                title: confirmation.title,
                details: confirmation.details,
                onCancel: { session.cancelAction() },
                onConfirm: { session.confirmAction() }
            )
            .transition(.opacity.combined(with: .move(edge: .bottom)))
        } else if let doneMessage = session.doneMessage {
            DoneCard(message: doneMessage)
                .transition(.opacity.combined(with: .scale(scale: 0.98)))
        } else if let reply = session.reply {
            MascotBubble(say: reply.say, steps: session.steps)
                .id(reply.say)
                .transition(.opacity.combined(with: .scale(scale: 0.98, anchor: .top)))
            CardsView(surfaces: session.surfaces, cards: reply.cards)
                .transition(.opacity.combined(with: .move(edge: .bottom)))
            if session.orb == .idle {
                // After the cards, never over them.
                IntentChips { session.ask($0) }
                    .padding(.horizontal, -Theme.Size.cardGutterMobile)
                    .transition(.opacity)
            }
        } else if session.transcript == nil {
            Welcome(listening: session.orb == .listening, handsFree: session.handsFree)
        }
        if let error = session.errorMessage {
            ErrorCard(
                message: error,
                contextText: session.transcript,
                onRetry: { session.ask(session.transcript ?? "Retry") },
                onCancel: { session.cancelAction() }
            )
            .transition(.opacity)
        }
    }

    // MARK: - Orb dock

    private var orbDock: some View {
        VStack(spacing: 6) {
            OrbView(state: session.orb, scale: hasTurn ? 0.72 : 1)
                .contentShape(Circle())
                .gesture(orbPress)
                .accessibilityAddTraits(.isButton)
                .accessibilityHint(orbHint)
                .accessibilityAction(named: "Type a question") { sheet = .debug }
                .frame(maxWidth: .infinity)
                .overlay(alignment: .trailing) {
                    Button {
                        sheet = .debug
                    } label: {
                        Image(systemName: "keyboard")
                            .font(.system(size: 18, weight: .medium))
                            .foregroundStyle(Theme.textPrimary)
                            .frame(width: Theme.Size.touchMin, height: Theme.Size.touchMin)
                            .glassSurface(.flat, cornerRadius: Theme.Radius.control, isInteractive: true)
                    }
                    .padding(.trailing, Theme.Size.cardGutterMobile)
                    .accessibilityLabel("Type a question")
                }
            OrbLabel(state: session.orb, label: orbLabel)
        }
        .padding(.bottom, 8)
        .frame(maxWidth: .infinity)
        .animation(Theme.Motion.standard, value: session.orb)
        .animation(Theme.Motion.standard, value: hasTurn)
    }

    private var hasTurn: Bool { session.transcript != nil || session.reply != nil || session.confirmation != nil || session.doneMessage != nil }

    /// Live: hold to talk, tap to stop the mascot (see `AgentSession.orbPressBegan`).
    /// Demo data: hold to type a question, as before there was a mic.
    private var orbPress: some Gesture {
        DragGesture(minimumDistance: 0)
            .onChanged { _ in
                guard !pressing else { return }
                pressing = true
                if session.connection == .fixtures {
                    debugHold = Task {
                        try? await Task.sleep(for: .seconds(0.5))
                        if !Task.isCancelled { sheet = .debug }
                    }
                } else {
                    session.orbPressBegan()
                }
            }
            .onEnded { _ in
                pressing = false
                debugHold?.cancel()
                session.orbPressEnded()
            }
    }

    private var orbHint: String {
        if session.connection == .fixtures { return "Touch and hold to type a question" }
        return session.handsFree ? "Just talk. Tap to stop the answer" : "Touch and hold to talk. Tap to stop the answer"
    }

    private var orbLabel: String? {
        if session.orb == .idle { return "Ready" }
        return session.label
    }
}

enum AppSheet: String, Identifiable {
    case settings, debug
    var id: String { rawValue }
}

// MARK: - Pieces

private struct Welcome: View {
    var listening = false
    var handsFree = false
    @Environment(\.typeScale) private var type

    var body: some View {
        VStack(alignment: .leading, spacing: 12) {
            Text(listening ? "Listening…" : "Ready")
                .font(type.display)
                .tracking(-1.44)
                .foregroundStyle(Theme.textPrimary)
            Text(hint)
                .font(type.body)
                .foregroundStyle(Theme.textMuted)
                .fixedSize(horizontal: false, vertical: true)
        }
        .padding(.top, 28)
        .padding(.horizontal, 4)
        .animation(Theme.Motion.standard, value: listening)
    }

    private var hint: String {
        switch (listening, handsFree) {
        case (true, false): "Ask your question, then let go of the orb."
        case (true, true): "Go ahead. I'll answer when you pause."
        case (false, false): "Look at something on your phone, then hold the orb and ask."
        case (false, true): "Look at something on your phone, then just ask."
        }
    }
}

/// What the mascot says (`reply.say`), plus the turn's tool steps as one quiet line.
struct MascotBubble: View {
    let say: String
    let steps: [String]

    @Environment(\.typeScale) private var type

    var body: some View {
        VStack(alignment: .leading, spacing: 12) {
            if !steps.isEmpty {
                HStack(spacing: 6) {
                    Image(systemName: "checkmark.circle.fill")
                        .font(type.meta)
                        .foregroundStyle(Theme.textPrimary)
                    Text(steps.map(Self.pastTense).joined(separator: " · "))
                        .font(type.meta)
                        .foregroundStyle(Theme.textSecondary)
                }
                .lineLimit(1)
            }
            Text(say)
                .font(type.answer)
                .tracking(type.answerTracking)
                .foregroundStyle(Theme.textPrimary)
                .fixedSize(horizontal: false, vertical: true)
        }
        .padding(Theme.Size.cardPadding)
        .frame(maxWidth: .infinity, alignment: .leading)
        .background(RoundedRectangle(cornerRadius: Theme.Radius.card, style: .continuous).fill(Theme.surface))
        .overlay(RoundedRectangle(cornerRadius: Theme.Radius.card, style: .continuous).strokeBorder(Theme.border, lineWidth: 1))
        .accessibilityElement(children: .combine)
    }

    /// "Checking trains…" → "Checked trains".
    static func pastTense(_ label: String) -> String {
        var text = label.trimmingCharacters(in: CharacterSet(charactersIn: "…. "))
        if let first = text.split(separator: " ").first, first.hasSuffix("ing") {
            let stem = first.dropLast(3)
            let past = stem.hasSuffix("e") ? stem + "d" : stem + "ed"
            text = String(past) + text.dropFirst(first.count)
        }
        return text
    }
}

/// Shown on `screen_ok`: what the server read from the latest screenshot (Context card).
struct ScreenChip: View {
